{"result": "{\n    \"title\": \"Calcium and Nutritional Health Community\",\n    \"summary\": \"The community focuses on the essential mineral calcium (CALCIO) and its relationships with various dietary components and health conditions. Key entities include dietary fiber (FIBRA DIETÉTICA), tobacco (TABACO), fortified foods (ALIMENTOS FORTIFICADOS), and dairy products (PRODUCTOS LÁCTEOS), all of which play significant roles in calcium metabolism and overall health.\",\n    \"rating\": 7.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is high due to the critical role of calcium in health and the significant public health implications of its deficiency and related conditions.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Calcium's role in bone health\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Calcium is a vital mineral essential for maintaining bone health and preventing diseases such as osteoporosis. Adequate calcium intake is crucial, especially for vulnerable populations like the elderly and children. The recommended daily intake varies, but guidelines suggest between 1000-1500 mg for most adults. Calcium's importance is underscored by its inclusion in parenteral nutrition solutions for patients unable to consume adequate nutrition orally, highlighting its necessity for metabolic health and bone development [Data: Entities (1991); Relationships (4681, 8239, 5325)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Impact of dietary fiber on calcium absorption\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Dietary fiber (FIBRA DIETÉTICA) plays a significant role in digestive health and can influence calcium metabolism. High fiber diets are associated with improved overall health, particularly in the elderly and children. Fiber can inhibit the absorption of certain nutrients, including calcium, which emphasizes the need for a balanced intake of both fiber and calcium-rich foods to ensure optimal health outcomes [Data: Entities (4827); Relationships (8253, 8394)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Tobacco's detrimental effects on calcium metabolism\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tobacco (TABACO) consumption is linked to negative health outcomes, particularly concerning bone health. Smoking is a known risk factor for osteoporosis, and avoiding tobacco is crucial for individuals requiring calcium supplementation. The relationship between tobacco use and calcium absorption highlights the importance of public health initiatives aimed at reducing smoking rates to improve overall health outcomes [Data: Entities (1291); Relationships (509, 6229)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Fortified foods as a strategy to combat calcium deficiency\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Fortified foods (ALIMENTOS FORTIFICADOS) are designed to enhance dietary calcium intake, particularly in at-risk populations. These foods are enriched with essential nutrients, including calcium and iron, to address common deficiencies. The fortification of foods is a public health strategy aimed at improving nutritional status and preventing health complications associated with inadequate calcium intake [Data: Entities (11513); Relationships (8275)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Dairy products as primary calcium sources\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Dairy products (PRODUCTOS LÁCTEOS) are recognized as a primary source of calcium, essential for bone health, especially in children. They contribute significantly to meeting the recommended calcium intake levels. However, the consumption of dairy must be balanced with considerations of saturated fat content, particularly in certain diets. The relationship between dairy intake and calcium levels is critical for maintaining strong bones and preventing osteoporosis [Data: Entities (7333); Relationships (8252)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Calcium's relationship with vitamin D\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Calcium (CALCIO) and vitamin D (VITAMINA D) are interdependent nutrients that play crucial roles in bone health. Vitamin D enhances calcium absorption in the intestines, making it essential for individuals with calcium deficiencies. This synergistic relationship is particularly important for elderly patients and those with conditions affecting nutrient absorption, such as celiac disease. Ensuring adequate levels of both nutrients is vital for preventing osteoporosis and other bone-related health issues [Data: Relationships (8237, 8384)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Calcium's role in preventing rickets\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Rickets (RAQUITISMO) is a condition caused by calcium deficiency, particularly in children, leading to weakened and deformed bones. The condition can also arise from malabsorption issues, emphasizing the need for adequate calcium intake in vulnerable populations. Preventing rickets through proper dietary management and supplementation is crucial for ensuring healthy bone development in children [Data: Entities (5683); Relationships (8249)].\"\n        }\n    ]\n}", "input": "\nYou are an AI assistant that helps a human analyst to perform general information discovery. Information discovery is the process of identifying and assessing relevant information associated with certain entities (e.g., organizations and individuals) within a network.\n\n# Goal\nWrite a comprehensive report of a community, given a list of entities that belong to the community as well as their relationships and optional associated claims. The report will be used to inform decision-makers about information associated with the community and their potential impact. The content of this report includes an overview of the community's key entities, their legal compliance, technical capabilities, reputation, and noteworthy claims.\n\n# Report Structure\n\nThe report should include the following sections:\n\n- TITLE: community's name that represents its key entities - title should be short but specific. When possible, include representative named entities in the title.\n- SUMMARY: An executive summary of the community's overall structure, how its entities are related to each other, and significant information associated with its entities.\n- IMPACT SEVERITY RATING: a float score between 0-10 that represents the severity of IMPACT posed by entities within the community.  IMPACT is the scored importance of a community.\n- RATING EXPLANATION: Give a single sentence explanation of the IMPACT severity rating.\n- DETAILED FINDINGS: A list of 5-10 key insights about the community. Each insight should have a short summary followed by multiple paragraphs of explanatory text grounded according to the grounding rules below. Be comprehensive.\n\nReturn output as a well-formed JSON-formatted string with the following format:\n    {{\n        \"title\": <report_title>,\n        \"summary\": <executive_summary>,\n        \"rating\": <impact_severity_rating>,\n        \"rating_explanation\": <rating_explanation>,\n        \"findings\": [\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_1_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_1_explanation>\n            }},\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_2_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_2_explanation>\n            }}\n        ]\n    }}\n\n# Grounding Rules\n\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n\"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids); <dataset name> (record ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X is the owner of Company Y and subject to many allegations of wrongdoing [Data: Reports (1), Entities (5, 7); Relationships (23); Claims (7, 2, 34, 64, 46, +more)].\"\n\nwhere 1, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, 46, and 64 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nDo not include information where the supporting evidence for it is not provided.\n\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nText:\n\nEntities\n\nid,entity,description\n5,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n6,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is an organization that is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n\nRelationships\n\nid,source,target,description\n37,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n38,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n39,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,The Unity March is taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n40,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,TRIBUNE SPOTLIGHT,Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity march taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n41,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,BAILEY ASADI,Bailey Asadi is speaking at Verdant Oasis Plaza about the march\n43,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,UNITY MARCH,Harmony Assembly is organizing the Unity March\n\nOutput:\n{{\n    \"title\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza and Unity March\",\n    \"summary\": \"The community revolves around the Verdant Oasis Plaza, which is the location of the Unity March. The plaza has relationships with the Harmony Assembly, Unity March, and Tribune Spotlight, all of which are associated with the march event.\",\n    \"rating\": 5.0,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is moderate due to the potential for unrest or conflict during the Unity March.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza as the central location\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza is the central entity in this community, serving as the location for the Unity March. This plaza is the common link between all other entities, suggesting its significance in the community. The plaza's association with the march could potentially lead to issues such as public disorder or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Harmony Assembly's role in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Unity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n1991,CALCIO,\"CALCIO, commonly known as calcium, is an essential mineral that plays a critical role in various bodily functions, particularly in maintaining bone health and development. It is vital for building and maintaining strong bones and teeth, and it also supports muscle function and nerve signaling. Adequate calcium intake is crucial for preventing conditions such as osteoporosis and osteomalacia, especially in older adults, children, and individuals with specific health conditions.\n\nCalcium is monitored in patients receiving parenteral nutrition to ensure proper metabolic function and is included in nutritional solutions for its importance in bone health and various physiological functions. Its absorption can be affected by several factors, including the presence of vitamin D, glucocorticoids, and certain gastrointestinal conditions, such as celiac disease and after gastric resection. \n\nThe recommended daily intake of calcium varies by age, sex, and activity level, with guidelines suggesting an intake between 1000-1500 mg for most adults. Special attention is given to populations at risk of deficiency, such as the elderly, individuals with lactose intolerance, and those undergoing treatments like bariatric surgery or steroid therapy. In these cases, calcium supplementation is often recommended to ensure adequate levels and prevent bone-related health issues.\n\nCalcium also plays a role in regulating blood pressure and may have protective effects against certain diseases, including some types of cancer. It is important for kidney health, as adequate calcium intake can help prevent kidney stones. However, its role in cardiovascular health remains a topic of debate.\n\nIn summary, CALCIO is a vital mineral essential for bone health, muscle function, and various other bodily processes. Its intake should be carefully managed, particularly in vulnerable populations, to prevent deficiencies and associated health complications.\",83\r\n1291,TABACO,\"TABACO refers to tobacco, a substance that is widely recognized for its negative health impacts. It is strongly advised to avoid tobacco consumption for at least 12 hours prior to medical tests to ensure accurate results, particularly in imaging procedures. The use of tobacco is discouraged due to its detrimental effects on bone health, as it is a known risk factor for osteoporosis. This is especially critical for patients with obesity and those undergoing bariatric surgery, as tobacco can exacerbate health complications in these groups. Furthermore, tobacco smoking has been established as a significant risk factor for the development of Graves' disease, with studies indicating an odds ratio of 3.5. Overall, tobacco consumption is a major public health concern, and health promotion programs often focus on reducing smoking rates to improve overall health outcomes.\",5\r\n4827,FIBRA DIETÉTICA,\"FIBRA DIETÉTICA refers to dietary fiber, a crucial component of nutrition that plays a significant role in promoting digestive health. It is found in various food sources, including whole grains, legumes, vegetables, and fruits. Dietary fiber aids in digestion, helps stabilize blood sugar levels, and contributes to the reduction of energy density in foods, which can promote feelings of fullness and assist in weight control.\n\nResearch indicates that dietary fiber is particularly beneficial for the elderly, as it is linked to improved overall health. Additionally, it is essential for children's diets, supporting their digestive health. As a type of carbohydrate that the body cannot digest, dietary fiber is important for gut health and is associated with various health benefits, including the potential to inhibit the absorption of adenine, which may lower uric acid levels.\n\nFIBRA DIETÉTICA is recognized in dietary recommendations and guidelines, such as those from the World Health Organization (WHO), emphasizing its importance in maintaining a balanced and healthy diet.\",17\r\n5683,RAQUITISMO,\"RAQUITISMO, también conocido como raquitismo, es una enfermedad metabólica ósea que afecta principalmente a los niños y resulta de la deficiencia de vitamina D. Esta condición se caracteriza por un desarrollo óseo inadecuado, lo que provoca la desmineralización en la placa de crecimiento y, como consecuencia, deformidades óseas. Además, el raquitismo puede desarrollarse en pacientes celíacos debido a la malabsorción de calcio y vitamina D, y también puede ser una complicación de la enfermedad de Wilson. En resumen, el raquitismo es una enfermedad que lleva a la formación de huesos blandos y débiles, afectando gravemente el crecimiento y desarrollo de los niños.\",8\r\n11513,ALIMENTOS FORTIFICADOS,\"ALIMENTOS FORTIFICADOS refers to fortified foods that have been enhanced with additional nutrients to improve their dietary value. These products typically include added nutrients such as calcium and iron, which are essential for preventing deficiencies, particularly in at-risk populations. The primary goal of fortifying these foods is to enhance their nutritional content and support better health outcomes by addressing common nutrient deficiencies. In summary, ALIMENTOS FORTIFICADOS are enriched foods designed to provide essential nutrients and improve overall dietary intake.\",4\r\n7333,PRODUCTOS LÁCTEOS,\"PRODUCTOS LÁCTEOS refer to a category of food items derived from milk, which includes products such as milk, cheese, yogurt, and butter. These dairy products are recognized as a primary source of essential nutrients, particularly calcium and vitamin D, which are crucial for children's dietary needs and overall health. They play a significant role in helping individuals meet their recommended intakes of these nutrients.\n\nIn addition to their nutritional benefits, dairy products have been studied for their effects on blood pressure and are associated with dietary quality and cardiovascular risk reduction. However, it is important to note that dairy products, especially in the European diet, can also be significant sources of saturated fat. Overall, while dairy products offer important health benefits, moderation and balance in consumption are key to maintaining a healthy diet.\",4\r\n11478,HUESO,\"HUESO, which translates to \"\"bone\"\" in English, serves as a major storage site for magnesium in the body, containing approximately 60% of the total body magnesium.\",2\r\n15358,ALIMENTOS RICOS EN CALCIO,\"Foods rich in calcium are recommended for maintaining adequate calcium levels in the body, especially in children and adolescents.\",1\r\n11515,CITRICOS,\"Citrus fruits are high in vitamin C, which aids in calcium absorption.\",1\r\n15351,VERDURAS DE HOJA VERDE,\"Leafy green vegetables are a good source of calcium, particularly those low in oxalates to enhance absorption\",1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n3330,PACIENTE,CALCIO,The patient requires monitoring of calcium levels to prevent deficiencies related to cystic fibrosis.,629\r\n4681,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,CALCIO,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL, which refers to the intravenous administration of nutrients, plays a critical role in the care of patients who cannot obtain adequate nutrition through oral means. A key component of this nutritional support is CALCIO (calcium), which is essential for maintaining bone health and supporting various physiological functions. Adequate calcium intake is particularly crucial for patients receiving parenteral nutrition to prevent bone-related issues, especially in pediatric patients who require calcium for proper development.\n\nCalcium is included in parenteral nutrition solutions to meet the body's mineral requirements, and it is recognized as a necessary supplement for these patients. However, the addition of calcium must be done with caution to avoid potential complications. Therefore, healthcare providers closely monitor and adjust calcium levels in patients receiving parenteral nutrition to ensure optimal metabolic health and prevent deficiencies. Overall, calcium is an indispensable mineral in parenteral nutrition, vital for the health and development of patients, particularly children.\",521\r\n509,PACIENTES,TABACO,\"Los pacientes deben evitar el tabaco para mejorar su salud, especialmente después de la cirugía\",232\r\n8239,CALCIO,VITAMINA D,\"CALCIO and VITAMINA D are both essential nutrients that play a critical role in maintaining bone health and preventing diseases such as osteoporosis. They are recommended to be taken together, as calcium supplementation should be paired with vitamin D to enhance absorption and overall effectiveness. Vitamin D significantly improves the bioavailability of calcium, which is particularly crucial for the bone health of elderly patients. A deficiency in vitamin D can lead to decreased intestinal absorption of calcium, highlighting its necessity for proper calcium absorption in the body. Furthermore, vitamin D supplementation is vital to ensure adequate calcium absorption, especially in individuals with lactose intolerance. In addition to its role in bone health, vitamin D also contributes to improving muscle function when combined with calcium. Overall, the synergistic relationship between CALCIO and VITAMINA D is essential for optimal metabolic processes and bone formation.\",157\r\n8282,CALCIO,NEFROLITIASIS,\"Calcium is a key factor in the development of kidney stones, particularly in cases of hypercalciuria\",157\r\n7029,CÁNCER,CALCIO,\"Calcium from dietary sources, particularly dairy, is inversely associated with digestive cancers.\",149\r\n5325,DIETA,CALCIO,The diet's calcium content is crucial for preventing osteoporosis,148\r\n6963,ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL,CALCIO,\"The entity \"\"ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL\"\" is closely related to \"\"CALCIO\"\" in the context of patient care and nutritional management. Calcio, a vital mineral, requires careful monitoring in patients suffering from enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal to prevent potential complications. The absorption of calcio can be significantly impaired in these patients, which may lead to a deficiency. Such a deficiency is particularly concerning as it can result in serious bone health issues in adults with enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal. Therefore, maintaining adequate levels of calcio is crucial for the overall health and well-being of individuals affected by this condition.\",140\r\n7450,PROTEÍNAS,CALCIO,\"High protein diets can affect calcium metabolism and excretion, influencing kidney stone risk\",140\r\n8237,CALCIO,MAGNESIO,\"Calcium and magnesium are both essential minerals that play crucial roles in maintaining bone health and supporting metabolism. They work together in various bodily functions, highlighting their interdependent relationship in nutrition. Their combined presence is vital for overall health, as they contribute to numerous physiological processes within the body.\",135\r\n5384,NUTRIENTES,CALCIO,Calcium is a vital nutrient for bone health and is classified as an essential nutrient,123\r\n8256,CALCIO,GALACTOSEMIA,\"Calcium is necessary for individuals with galactosemia, especially during lactation, and is provided through soy formulas.\",122\r\n8299,CALCIO,LACTANCIA,\"CALCIO (calcium) and LACTANCIA (lactation) are interconnected in terms of dietary recommendations. Calcium has specific recommended intake levels for infants during lactation, highlighting the importance of adequate calcium consumption for this age group. Additionally, lactation provides dietary reference intake guidelines for calcium, which are tailored for different age groups, ensuring that individuals receive appropriate nutritional guidance throughout various stages of development. Together, these insights emphasize the critical role of calcium during the lactation period and the necessity of adhering to established dietary guidelines.\",120\r\n8172,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL (NP),CALCIO,La nutrición parenteral debe incluir calcio en cantidades adecuadas para el soporte nutricional,114\r\n8259,CALCIO,INSUFICIENCIA RENAL AGUDA,\"El calcio es esencial para los pacientes en diálisis, quienes necesitan suplementos debido a la falta de vitamina D\",111\r\n8289,CALCIO,DEPORTISTAS,Los deportistas necesitan un consumo adecuado de calcio para mantener la masa ósea y prevenir la osteoporosis.,110\r\n8300,CALCIO,DRI 971,Calcio is one of the minerals with recommended daily intake levels outlined in DRI 971,110\r\n8269,CALCIO,HIPERCALCEMIA,\"CALCIO and HIPERCALCEMIA are closely related, as hipercalcemia is defined by elevated levels of calcium in the blood. This condition indicates a direct relationship between the two entities, highlighting that high serum calcium levels can pose significant health risks.\",107\r\n8265,CALCIO,HTA,Calcium intake has been studied for its potential effects on blood pressure in individuals with hypertension.,106\r\n8250,CALCIO,SÍNDROME METABÓLICO,\"El consumo de calcio se ha asociado con una menor incidencia de síndrome metabólico, indicando una relación\",104\r\n8251,CALCIO,YODO,Ambos nutrientes son esenciales en la dieta y se discuten en el contexto de la salud pública y la nutrición en España.,103\r\n7159,TRASPLANTE HEPÁTICO,CALCIO,Calcium supplementation is recommended for liver transplant patients to support bone health,103\r\n8011,FÓSFORO,CALCIO,\"FÓSFORO and CALCIO are two essential minerals that play a critical role in bone metabolism. Both minerals are often monitored together, particularly in newborns, to ensure proper development and health. It is important to note that excessive intake of phosphorus can negatively affect calcium absorption, which in turn can impact overall bone health. This relationship highlights the need for a balanced intake of both minerals, as an excess of phosphorus may lead to decreased calcium absorption, further emphasizing the interconnectedness of FÓSFORO and CALCIO in maintaining healthy bones.\",102\r\n8268,CALCIO,HIPOCALCEMIA,\"La hipocalcemia se relaciona directamente con niveles bajos de calcio en el suero, lo que afecta la salud del paciente.\",101\r\n8253,CALCIO,FIBRA DIETÉTICA,Calcium and dietary fiber are both nutrients studied for their roles in weight management and body composition.,100\r\n7543,HOMBRES,CALCIO,Men have specific dietary recommendations for Calcium intake,100\r\n1742,SARCOPENIA,FIBRA DIETÉTICA,\"Dietary fiber can positively affect digestive health, which is crucial for overall health in the elderly, potentially impacting sarcopenia\",100\r\n8301,CALCIO,NUTRICION PARENTERAL,Calcio is included in parenteral nutrition solutions for bone health and cellular functions,99\r\n8241,CALCIO,HIPOCALEMIA,\"CALCIO and HIPOCALEMIA are closely related entities, particularly in the context of medical treatment. Calcium supplementation is often necessary in the treatment of HIPOCALEMIA, which is a condition characterized by low calcium levels in the body. This condition is especially significant in newborns, as HIPOCALEMIA is directly related to calcium levels in this population, indicating a strong relationship between calcium levels and the health of newborns. Thus, maintaining adequate CALCIO levels is crucial for preventing and managing HIPOCALEMIA.\",98\r\n8284,CALCIO,EII,Patients with EII often require calcium supplementation to prevent osteoporosis due to dietary restrictions,98\r\n8240,CALCIO,PACIENTE ANCIANO,\"El Calcio es esencial para la salud ósea del paciente anciano, y su déficit puede llevar a osteoporosis.\",97\r\n8245,CALCIO,MOTHER,La madre aumenta la absorción de calcio para facilitar el desarrollo esquelético del feto,95\r\n8254,CALCIO,MICRONUTRIENT DEFICIENCY,Calcium deficiency is another common micronutrient deficiency that can occur after bariatric surgery,94\r\n8302,CALCIO,SMOFKABIVEN CENTRAL,SmofKabiven Central contains calcium as an essential electrolyte for parenteral nutrition,93\r\n8267,CALCIO,CALCITONINA,La calcitonina actúa para reducir los niveles de calcio en la sangre al inhibir la reabsorción ósea y aumentar la excreción urinaria de calcio.,92\r\n8249,CALCIO,RAQUITISMO,\"Calcio, or calcium, is an essential mineral that plays a crucial role in the mineralization of bones. A deficiency in calcium can lead to raquitismo, known as rickets, which is characterized by the inadequate mineralization of bones, resulting in weakened and deformed skeletal structures. Additionally, raquitismo can also be caused by the malabsorption of calcium, particularly in patients with celiac disease, where the body's ability to absorb this vital mineral is compromised. Thus, maintaining adequate levels of calcium is essential to prevent raquitismo and ensure proper bone health.\",91\r\n8287,CALCIO,MINERALES Y OLIGOELEMENTOS,Calcium is a key mineral that is often discussed in the context of overall mineral supplementation,91\r\n8394,VITAMINA D,FIBRA DIETÉTICA,Vitamin D and dietary fiber are both important nutrients that have been researched for their effects on health and weight management.,91\r\n8266,CALCIO,HORMONA PARATIROIDEA,\"La hormona paratiroidea actúa para aumentar los niveles de calcio en la sangre, regulando su liberación del hueso y su reabsorción en el riñón.\",90\r\n8285,CALCIO,CALCITRIOL,\"Calcitriol is used to aid calcium absorption in patients, particularly those with osteoporosis\",90\r\n8255,CALCIO,DIETAS VEGETARIANAS,Calcium is an important nutrient that may require special attention in vegetarian diets to ensure adequate intake,89\r\n6229,TABACO,CALCIO,\"TABACO and CALCIO are interconnected in the context of bone health. Avoiding tobacco is crucial for minimizing the risk of osteoporosis in patients who require calcium supplementation. The consumption of tobacco negatively impacts bone health and the absorption of calcium, highlighting the importance of steering clear of tobacco to support overall skeletal integrity and ensure effective calcium utilization.\",88\r\n8275,CALCIO,ALIMENTOS FORTIFICADOS,Fortified foods are designed to increase calcium intake in the diet,87\r\n8246,CALCIO,HORMONA PARATIROIDEA (PTH),\"PTH regulates calcium levels in the blood, promoting calcium release from bones and increasing calcium reabsorption in the kidneys.\",87\r\n8248,CALCIO,OSTEOMALACIA ONCOGÉNICA,\"La deficiencia de calcio puede contribuir a la osteomalacia, que es un síntoma de la osteomalacia oncogénica.\",87\r\n8252,CALCIO,PRODUCTOS LÁCTEOS,\"CALCIO and PRODUCTOS LÁCTEOS are closely related, as dairy products are recognized as a primary source of calcium, which is essential for bone health, particularly in children. This highlights the importance of incorporating dairy products into the diet to ensure adequate calcium intake for maintaining strong bones.\",87\r\n8274,CALCIO,HUESO,Calcium is essential for strengthening bones and preventing osteoporosis,85\r\n8298,CALCIO,ADOLESCENTES,\"Adolescents have increased calcium needs due to growth, making calcium-rich foods essential\",85\r\n8297,CALCIO,ALIMENTOS RICOS EN CALCIO,Foods rich in calcium are necessary to maintain adequate calcium levels in the body,84\r\n8276,CALCIO,CITRICOS,\"Citrus fruits provide vitamin C, which helps in the absorption of calcium\",84\r\n8294,CALCIO,VERDURAS DE HOJA VERDE,Leafy green vegetables are recommended as a supplementary source of calcium,84\r\n8384,VITAMINA D,RAQUITISMO,\"VITAMINA D and RAQUITISMO are closely related, particularly in the context of health conditions such as celiac disease. Rickets, a condition characterized by weak and soft bones, is primarily caused by a deficiency in vitamin D. In patients with celiac disease, the malabsorption of vitamin D can contribute to the development of rickets. Therefore, ensuring adequate levels of vitamin D is crucial in preventing rickets, especially in individuals who may have absorption issues due to gastrointestinal disorders.\",82\r\n7028,CÁNCER,PRODUCTOS LÁCTEOS,\"Dairy products have been associated with a reduced risk of various cancers, including colorectal and breast cancer.\",70\r\n5341,DIETA,TABACO,La dieta recomendada implica evitar el consumo de tabaco para asegurar resultados precisos en las pruebas,70\r\n5383,NUTRIENTES,FIBRA DIETÉTICA,Dietary fiber is an important nutrient for digestive health,57\r\n8320,MAGNESIO,HUESO,\"Bone serves as a major reservoir for magnesium, containing a significant portion of the body's total magnesium\",54\r\n8656,HIERRO,ALIMENTOS FORTIFICADOS,Fortified foods are enriched with iron to help prevent iron deficiency and related health issues,49\r\n9249,ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON,RAQUITISMO,\"El raquitismo puede presentarse en pacientes con enfermedad de Wilson, afectando el desarrollo óseo\",49\r\n13476,GLP-1,FIBRA DIETÉTICA,\"Dietary fiber can influence the secretion of GLP-1, which regulates appetite and energy balance.\",41\r\n13166,DIABETES TIPO 2,FIBRA DIETÉTICA,\"La ingesta de fibra dietética se asocia inversamente con el desarrollo de diabetes tipo 2, donde un mayor consumo puede reducir el riesgo de esta enfermedad.\",40\r\n16437,PRODUCTOS LÁCTEOS,HTA,\"Dairy products have been studied for their potential effects on blood pressure, with mixed results.\",27\r\n14107,FIBRA DIETÉTICA,CÁNCER COLORRECTAL,\"La ingesta de fibra dietética se ha asociado con una reducción del riesgo de cáncer colorrectal, donde un mayor consumo puede disminuir este riesgo.\",26\r\n14109,FIBRA DIETÉTICA,CÁNCER PANCREÁTICO,\"La relación entre el consumo de fibra dietética y el riesgo de cáncer pancreático es inconsistente, lo que sugiere que no hay una asociación clara.\",21\r\n14113,FIBRA DIETÉTICA,FÓRMULAS ESPECÍFICAS,Specific formulas often include dietary fiber to aid in digestion,21\r\n6228,TABACO,ENFERMEDAD DE GRAVES,El tabaquismo se ha asociado con un mayor riesgo de desarrollar la enfermedad de Graves.,20\r\n8344,FOSFATO,RAQUITISMO,Fosfato deficiency contributes to raquitismo by affecting the crystallization process in bones,15\r\n15123,RAQUITISMO,OSTEOMALACIA ONCOGÉNICA,El raquitismo y la osteomalacia oncogénica comparten características similares en cuanto a la mineralización ósea deficient